Theorem RL-13: REMOVED — Construct + Once does NOT imply RC == 1 at death (removal confirmation)

  Preconditions:
    - RL-13 was REMOVED from Annex E §AIMS Allocation Reuse (same root
      cause as the removed DP-10). The former rule claimed
      `Construct + Cardinality = Once => RC == 1 at death`.
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; this is the CONFIRMATION entry
      the sec-01 Realization.proof RL-13 row points at (no theorem skeleton
      to discharge — the obligation is to confirm the removal is sound).
    - Root cause of the removal: one use of a Construct + Once value may be
      "store into a data structure", which creates an alias via RcInc — so
      Construct + Once alone does NOT guarantee the value is the sole owner
      (RC == 1) at death.
    - Subsumed by: the Uniqueness dimension (§AIMS §3.4) as the direct source
      of truth for reuse eligibility, and DP-6 + RL-11 + RL-12 reuse gating
      via Uniqueness.
    - Per the sec-08 Per-RL Proof-Status Tracking table, RL-13 carries the
      terminal `n/a - removed` proof_status (exempt from the active-rule
      enum); this proof confirms the removal closed the unsoundness.

  Soundness property:
    The removal of RL-13 is sound iff reuse eligibility is established SOLELY
    via the Uniqueness dimension (DP-6 + RL-11 / RL-12), and the
    Construct + Once heuristic is NEVER permitted as a reuse gate:

      (C1) A Construct + Once value that has been aliased (stored into a
           structure -> MaybeShared / Shared) is NOT statically Unique, so
           it is NOT reuse-eligible-for-in-place under RL-11 (which requires
           Unique). The removed RL-13 heuristic would have wrongly admitted
           it on Construct + Once alone.

      (C2) `Construct + Cardinality = Once` does NOT imply `Uniqueness =
           Unique` at death — the only sound reuse gate is the Uniqueness
           dimension itself.

    Confirming (C1) + (C2) demonstrates the removal eliminated the DP-10
    root-cause unsoundness without leaving a residual reuse path that
    bypasses the Uniqueness proof.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the case_analysis engine — a confirmation that
    the removed heuristic is NOT reachable as a reuse gate.

    Part (C1) — aliased Construct+Once is not Unique:
      The verifier confirms an aliased (MaybeShared) Construct + Once value
      is not equal to Unique — RL-11 / RL-12 (which require dying-Unique)
      reject it; only the runtime IsShared branch (RL-11a) handles a
      MaybeShared candidate, never the Construct + Once heuristic.

    Part (C2) — Construct + Once does not imply Unique:
      The verifier confirms the removed claim
      (`Construct + Once => Unique`) is NOT asserted anywhere — reuse
      eligibility flows only through DP-6 + the Uniqueness dimension.

      Coverage gate: 2 confirmation cases.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY —
        section_08::verify_rl13_removal_confirmation; confirms the
        Construct + Once heuristic is not reachable as a reuse gate; emits
        Fail if the removed unsound claim were reintroduced)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges the RL-13 removal confirmation — (C1) an aliased Construct+Once value is not statically Unique so RL-11/RL-12 reject it and (C2) Construct + Once does not imply Unique at death — confirming reuse eligibility flows solely through the Uniqueness dimension (DP-6 + RL-11/RL-12), closing the DP-10 root-cause unsoundness
